# Module 06 — Budget Review, Approval and Finalization
# Tester: Ekow | Audience: Budget Team

AUTH standard-login
MODULE budgeting

# NOTE: Tests in this module that use the Review page navigate to it
# in STEPS (or SETUP). The MODULE only gets us to the budgeting dashboard.

---

TEST P-01: Open the Review page for a PENDING budget

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel

STEPS
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load

ASSERT
  url contains "/review"
  "Review Process" is visible in breadcrumb
  "Budgeted Fees" is visible in sidebar
  "Collections" is visible in sidebar
  "Priority Areas" is visible in sidebar
  "Permitted Institutions" is visible in sidebar
  "sections need attention" is visible

# DISCOVERY: This reveals a tension with Module 05 P-27.
# Module 05 P-27 says clicking "Review" opens a modal with "Confirm Review".
# Module 06 P-01 says the same button navigates to a full page.
# These describe the same button but expect different results.
# Either: (a) the test in Module 05 compressed the full flow into two steps,
# or (b) there are two different UI paths. This needs to be verified during testing.

---

TEST P-08: Verify the Budgeted Fees section (with notes)

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load

STEPS
  click "Budgeted Fees" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  type "Cross-checked with finance spreadsheet" into "Notes"
  click "Confirm Verification"

ASSERT
  toast shows "Section verified successfully"
  "Budgeted Fees" in sidebar shows "verified"
  "Verify" is disabled

---

TEST P-13: Sidebar shows all sections verified when all 4 are verified

# Depends on: sections having been verified in prior tests or via SETUP.
# This test verifies the final UI state — the green banner.

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load
  # Verify all 4 sections
  click "Budgeted Fees" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"
  click "Collections" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"
  click "Priority Areas" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"
  click "Permitted Institutions" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"

ASSERT
  "All sections verified" is visible
  "sections need attention" is not visible

# SPEC GAP: SETUP is getting long here. In reality these verification steps ARE
# test steps. This pattern suggests we may need a way to declare test dependencies:
#   DEPENDS ON P-08, P-10, P-11, P-12
# so the executor can run prerequisite tests before this one rather than
# duplicating all the setup steps inline.

---

TEST P-14: Confirm Review — move budget from PENDING to REVIEWED

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load
  # Ensure all 4 sections are verified before attempting Confirm Review

STEPS
  click "Confirm Review"

ASSERT
  toast shows "Budget successfully marked as Reviewed"
  url is "/budgeting"
  status badge equals "REVIEWED"

---

TEST P-16: Approve a REVIEWED budget with all requirements met

SETUP
  select first budget with status "REVIEWED" from left panel

STEPS
  click "Approve" in action bar

ASSERT
  all requirements show "verified" in checklist
  "Confirm Approval" is enabled

STEPS
  click "Confirm Approval"

ASSERT
  toast contains "successfully"
  status badge equals "APPROVED"
  "Finalize" is visible in action bar

# SPEC GAP: Two STEPS/ASSERT blocks in one test. Some tests naturally have a
# mid-test assertion (observe something, then act on it). We need to decide:
# allow multiple STEPS/ASSERT pairs per TEST, or split into separate tests.
# Splitting is cleaner but loses the sequential narrative.

---

TEST P-19: Finalize an APPROVED budget

SETUP
  select first budget with status "APPROVED" from left panel

STEPS
  click "Finalize" in action bar
  click "Finalize Now"

ASSERT
  toast contains "successfully"
  status badge equals "FINALIZED"
  "Finalize" is not visible in action bar

---

TEST N-01: Attempt to Confirm Review when not all sections are verified

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load
  # Verify only 2 of 4 sections
  click "Budgeted Fees" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"
  click "Collections" in sidebar
  click "Verify"
  click "Confirm Verification"

STEPS
  click "Confirm Review"

ASSERT
  error shows "Please verify all sections before completing the review"
  url contains "/review"
  status badge does not equal "REVIEWED"

# SPEC GAP: "status badge does not equal" — we need a negation variant for content assertions.

---

TEST N-07: Confirm Review is disabled for user without ChangeStatus permission

AUTH restricted-reviewer
# Requires: auth/restricted-reviewer.axtest — a user who can VERIFY sections
# (has ApprovedFeesChecked etc.) but lacks Budgets.ChangeStatus permission.

SETUP
  select first budget with status "PENDING" from left panel
  click "Review" in action bar
  wait for page to load

ASSERT
  "Confirm Review" is disabled

---

TEST E-07: Approval modal text changes between unmet and met requirements

SETUP
  select first budget with status "REVIEWED" from left panel

STEPS
  click "Approve" in action bar

ASSERT
  "Action Required" is visible
  "Confirm Approval" is disabled

STEPS
  dismiss dialog
  # Fix the missing requirement — for this test, assume fees are unverified.
  # In a real run this would involve going to the review page and verifying the section.
  # This edge case test is best verified manually or via a dedicated fixture.

# SPEC NOTE: Some edge case tests that verify mid-flow UI state changes are
# difficult to fully automate without test fixtures that create specific data states.
# These are good candidates for "semi-automated" tests in V1 — automate what we can,
# note what requires a specific pre-existing data state.
